<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements, applied ONLY on the Developer ID / notarization
  path (`make notarize`, or `make app CODESIGN_IDENTITY="Developer ID …"`).
  The ad-hoc and self-signed paths ignore this file.

  dBrief is NOT App-Sandboxed. The ad-hoc/self-signed builds reach TCC-protected
  resources from the Info.plist usage strings alone, so this was originally empty
  of resource entitlements — but that was WRONG for the hardened runtime. Under
  the hardened runtime, a few privacy resources are ALSO gated by a resource-access
  entitlement, and access is denied (the System Settings toggle won't take) without
  it, EVEN though the app isn't sandboxed and the usage string is present. The split
  is observable: Screen Recording + Speech Recognition are TCC-only (no entitlement,
  always worked), while Microphone + Calendar + Reminders need the keys below.

  Resource access (REQUIRED under hardened runtime, or mic/calendar/reminders break):
  - device.audio-input: AVAudioEngine / AVCaptureDevice microphone capture.
  - personal-information.calendars: EventKit calendar matching (auto-fill title/attendees).
  - personal-information.reminders: EventKit "Apple Reminders" integration (one per action item).

  Runtime exceptions for the on-device ML stack:
  - allow-jit / allow-unsigned-executable-memory: MLX + Metal generate and run
    JIT code on the GPU/CPU path.
  - disable-library-validation: the app loads the separately-built dBriefMLHost
    helper and dlopen's bundled frameworks/dylibs (MLX, WhisperKit, FluidAudio)
    that aren't signed by the same Team ID.

  If notarization later flags additional issues (e.g. the audit log mentions
  another restricted capability), add the corresponding key here and re-run.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.personal-information.calendars</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.personal-information.reminders</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
